But wait: `campaignFocus` object in useRunView is recreated each render, and `focus` is stable. That's campaign. For placements, effect deps [selected, placements]. `selected` is a state object stable unless select called. So re-runs only when placements identity changes: after second rankPlacements (post agent). That's once — but it happens maybe seconds after clicking, and yanks you back once. Still buggy but "keep sucking you back"?

Also scrollIntoView with behavior smooth: when map is scrolled into view, on mobile the layout... Hmm "keep sucking you back to it" suggests repeated. What could re-trigger repeatedly? The `at` timestamp in the selected object is used for scroll into view in the list (map selection). Let me look at PlacementsSection scroll effect (line ~111 onwards) which scrolls row into view when from map. That's the list. But clicking list → map. Maybe interplay: clicking a placement marker in the list, scroll map into view on phones. Then user scrolls back down... And PlacementsSection effect for selected from map only.

Actually wait — is there another possibility: focus.select on list row; effect scrolls map into view. Browsers scrollIntoView on element inside a scroll container. On desktop layout map and list side by side, scrolling map into view might scroll the whole page, which scrolls list too? Not repeatedly though.

Another repeated trigger: `placements` array recreated by `ordered` useMemo each time `run` reference changes — run changes on each agent event (many events during the run). During the agent run, new events arrive => new run => new ordered => new placements (same content, new identity) => effect reruns => flyTo + scrollIntoView. That's the "keep sucking you back": if you click a placement while the agent is still streaming events, every incoming event yanks you back. Fix: guard so the effect only acts once per selection.

